WEBVTT

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:20.180
I'm out of here!

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:23.420
"Out of here?"
What happened to you all of a sudden?

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:26.450
Miyao! You said you would teach me
the meaning of "progress"

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:28.420
as a high school student!

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:33.830
<i>It looks like that boy Miyao couldn't take
the vibe in this room.</i>

00:00:34.330 --> 00:00:37.330
<i>Or maybe he knows
the truth behind what's going on here.</i>

00:00:38.230 --> 00:00:43.240
<i>Why do I feel my chest tighten
when I look at this girl?</i>

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:44.540
<i>Wait,</i>

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:46.880
<i>does this girl like Haruo?</i>

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:52.310
<i>You must be kidding!
They're still first-year high schoolers!</i>

00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:57.520
<i>I'm 19 but I've never even fallen in love,
let alone been in a love triangle!</i>

00:00:58.590 --> 00:01:01.390
<i>My own sister Akira just stares off
into space,</i>

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:04.430
<i>so how did she get ahead of me in this?</i>

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:07.060
<i>This is so depraved!</i>

00:01:07.630 --> 00:01:09.800
<i>If I stay in this sordid place too long,</i>

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:12.970
<i>my pure heart will become soiled!</i>

00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:18.240
What? Where are you going, Makoto?

00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:22.510
I'm feeling faint, so I'm going downstairs
to chat with your mother.

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:24.480
Are you all right?

00:01:24.650 --> 00:01:26.850
<i>Goddamn this freaking perv!</i>

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:29.420
What the heck was that for?

00:01:32.890 --> 00:01:36.420
ORIGINAL WORK BY RENSUKE OSHIKIRI

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:09.050
Oh, Makoto. What's the matter?

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:12.050
It's a sordid, sleazy mess upstairs.

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:15.790
What? It's a sordid, sleazy mess upstairs?

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:20.760
I don't understand it. I'm just a child,
so I don't understand it at all.

00:03:20.830 --> 00:03:24.030
It's all right, you poor thing.

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:27.540
Why don't the two of us
continue playing disgusting word chain?

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:28.940
Yes! I'm up for that!

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:32.070
<i>What the heck is with this vibe?</i>

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:35.240
<i>It's like a battlefield
between competing wills!</i>

00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:39.350
<i>Like the overwhelmingly bloodthirsty vibe
of the combat arena!</i>

00:03:39.910 --> 00:03:42.880
I... was going to say earlier...

00:03:44.150 --> 00:03:47.560
I've been wanting to play
a fighting game against you, Ono.

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:48.990
<i>A match?</i>

00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:51.930
Yaguchi, did you buy <i>Virtua Fighter 2</i>
for the Saturn?

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:54.000
Yes, of course.

00:03:55.030 --> 00:03:57.230
I don't mind you fighting each other,

00:03:57.300 --> 00:03:59.830
but I've only got one joystick here.

00:04:08.210 --> 00:04:12.010
<i>I can't believe Ono and Hidaka are
suddenly battling it out here!</i>

00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:15.180
<i>But this will be worth watching.</i>

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:25.190
<i>I never thought that
I would be able to fight Ono here today.</i>

00:04:25.830 --> 00:04:28.000
<i>Will she come at me playfully? Or...</i>

00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:32.500
<i>Yoshi Senrin, then a series
of combos when she's stunned!</i>

00:04:32.570 --> 00:04:34.070
<i>Then a Byakko Soushouda!</i>

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:38.940
<i>She's totally serious about this!
I lost a ton of stamina already!</i>

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:40.410
<i>That was a Honshin Tanda!</i>

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:43.680
<i>She crushed me!</i>

00:04:45.750 --> 00:04:48.220
<i>She stayed silent after losing.
This is a real fight!</i>

00:04:52.350 --> 00:04:53.350
<i>Tanyokuchou!</i>

00:04:54.290 --> 00:04:55.560
<i>High Roundhouse Kick!</i>

00:04:56.690 --> 00:04:57.530
<i>Gaimon Chouchuu!</i>

00:04:57.590 --> 00:04:59.260
<i>Roundhouse Punch!</i>

00:05:00.190 --> 00:05:02.960
<i>No matter how much I hit,
she blocks them with her moves.</i>

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:06.370
<i>It's as if Ono's will is
manifesting itself in her fighting.</i>

00:05:06.930 --> 00:05:08.540
<i>She sees right through me!</i>

00:05:10.170 --> 00:05:11.240
<i>Souhakushu!</i>

00:05:11.310 --> 00:05:13.980
<i>Low Roundhouse Kick! I can't lose this!</i>

00:05:14.440 --> 00:05:18.410
<i>Yaguchi doesn't matter right now!
I want to win this as a gamer!</i>

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:21.220
<i>Hidaka's fighting back!</i>

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:23.420
<i>This is a battle of wills between women!</i>

00:05:23.720 --> 00:05:26.450
-<i>How can you be so unconcerned, man?</i>
-That hurts!

00:05:30.490 --> 00:05:32.730
<i>She's totally serious.
She can't stand to lose!</i>

00:05:33.190 --> 00:05:34.800
<i>She's always silent!</i>

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:38.630
<i>When did these two get so good at this?</i>

00:05:39.430 --> 00:05:41.100
<i>Where have they been practicing?</i>

00:05:48.940 --> 00:05:51.210
<i>She doesn't want me to think
the gamepad is a handicap.</i>

00:05:51.750 --> 00:05:53.510
<i>Ono really is amazing!</i>

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:57.120
<i>But I've also gained plenty of experience!</i>

00:05:57.920 --> 00:05:59.590
<i>I swear I won't back down!</i>

00:06:02.760 --> 00:06:05.030
<i>Hougeki Unshin Soukoshou!</i>

00:06:08.660 --> 00:06:10.500
<i>You're ten years too early to face me!</i>

00:06:12.170 --> 00:06:15.470
<i>The three-move combo of Bonken,
Yoshi Senrin, then Soushou,</i>

00:06:15.540 --> 00:06:17.640
<i>otherwise known as the Akira Special!</i>

00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:22.240
<i>I've been defeated.</i>

00:06:30.620 --> 00:06:33.090
Ono, can we fight again sometime?

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:35.660
I want to show you I can win.

00:06:38.530 --> 00:06:41.330
What? You want to show you can win what?

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:42.530
At a video game.

00:06:45.570 --> 00:06:46.770
What was that for?

00:06:49.670 --> 00:06:50.640
What was that all about?

00:06:50.940 --> 00:06:54.380
Akira! Don't leave your sister behind!

00:06:54.940 --> 00:06:57.110
She's as mysterious as ever.

00:06:57.550 --> 00:06:59.880
<i>That's right. Women are mysterious.</i>

00:07:00.680 --> 00:07:02.720
<i>And solving that mystery is</i>

00:07:03.350 --> 00:07:04.490
<i>a man's duty.</i>

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:17.330
<i>This is Sol Smasher hell!</i>

00:07:17.730 --> 00:07:20.470
<i>He keeps blasting them at me
without shame!</i>

00:07:23.400 --> 00:07:26.310
Feel free to use
your Oni Kubi Hineri forever.

00:07:26.710 --> 00:07:28.310
If you can get close enough.

00:07:28.380 --> 00:07:31.410
Whenever we come to fight you,

00:07:31.480 --> 00:07:33.610
we'll always use Pyron.

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:36.920
We hope you get sick and tired
of facing Pyron.

00:07:36.980 --> 00:07:39.050
Why are you pulling this crap?

00:07:39.120 --> 00:07:43.590
It's punishment for crushing the heart of
our sweet darling, Hidaka.

00:07:43.660 --> 00:07:46.530
You will suffer for it
on the video screen.

00:07:46.990 --> 00:07:51.930
You guys must be part of that
Team Mizonokuchi led by Nikotama Felicia.

00:07:52.730 --> 00:07:56.670
You know, I always play in Mizonokuchi
so I'm part of Team Mizonokuchi too!

00:07:57.610 --> 00:07:59.010
You're not one of us.

00:07:59.310 --> 00:08:02.280
Any gamer that's loved by a woman
isn't a real gamer!

00:08:02.740 --> 00:08:03.980
That's just dumb!

00:08:04.050 --> 00:08:07.780
Hey, you guys!
What are you all ganging up on him for?

00:08:07.850 --> 00:08:10.750
You know it's our rule
to get along with other players, right?

00:08:11.120 --> 00:08:14.520
Jeez! You sure hang out with
a weird crowd, Hidaka.

00:08:15.190 --> 00:08:17.560
This place used to be
a cool place to chill.

00:08:17.630 --> 00:08:19.460
Now it's just a place for bullies.

00:08:20.060 --> 00:08:23.160
You're right about that.
Ono hasn't come by lately either.

00:08:23.700 --> 00:08:26.170
What? Why bring up Ono?

00:08:26.230 --> 00:08:27.100
Oh, I don't know.

00:08:27.770 --> 00:08:28.900
Whatever.

00:08:28.970 --> 00:08:31.070
Hidaka, let's play <i>Virtua Fighter 2</i>.

00:08:31.140 --> 00:08:32.840
We'll see who's better,

00:08:32.910 --> 00:08:34.840
-your Sarah or my Kage...
-Not today.

00:08:34.910 --> 00:08:37.650
I would rather play
<i>Samurai Shodown III: Blades of Blood</i>.

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:39.580
Hey, you little punk.

00:08:40.010 --> 00:08:41.980
If you pester Miss Hidaka too much,

00:08:42.050 --> 00:08:45.720
you'll get a taste of my 60-kilogram punch
I've hammered the punching machine with.

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:46.690
Sixty kilograms?

00:08:47.190 --> 00:08:50.690
My 32-kilogram grip strength is
nothing to scoff at!

00:08:50.760 --> 00:08:51.860
Isn't that below average?

00:08:53.790 --> 00:08:56.960
Me and my 90-kilogram back strength
are pretty damn formidable too.

00:08:57.030 --> 00:08:58.970
These guys are actually pretty hilarious.

00:08:59.430 --> 00:09:02.270
Miss Hidaka is saying that
she doesn't want you around!

00:09:02.340 --> 00:09:04.540
How come you can't understand that?

00:09:04.610 --> 00:09:06.210
Isn't that right, Miss Hidaka?

00:09:07.310 --> 00:09:08.680
You may be right.

00:09:08.740 --> 00:09:11.680
JOY METER

00:09:12.610 --> 00:09:15.380
Is that so? Fine, I'll leave for now.

00:09:15.850 --> 00:09:17.790
Just you wait, you dumb Team Mizonokuchi!

00:09:21.460 --> 00:09:22.460
What a joke!

00:09:22.520 --> 00:09:25.190
Hey, Koharu. That's not cool.

00:09:25.260 --> 00:09:27.900
It's not like you
to say mean things like that.

00:09:28.760 --> 00:09:32.530
Lately, whenever I'm around Yaguchi,
I feel so mean-spirited.

00:09:33.270 --> 00:09:37.540
I suddenly want to slap him in the face
and kick the crap out of him.

00:09:39.040 --> 00:09:42.510
<i>I wonder if playing fighting games
all the time awakened her sadistic side.</i>

00:09:43.280 --> 00:09:47.650
<i>What is this? I don't understand
what these pent-up feelings inside me are.</i>

00:09:53.620 --> 00:09:55.790
<i>Goddamn it! This really ticks me off!</i>

00:09:56.320 --> 00:09:58.960
<i>Team Mizonokuchi, my ass!
What a bunch of butt-kissers!</i>

00:09:59.830 --> 00:10:01.800
<i>Fighting games are a competitive world!</i>

00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:04.600
<i>They're a brutal battlefield
where winners and losers are decided!</i>

00:10:05.070 --> 00:10:07.270
<i>That's exactly why
you have to be independent!</i>

00:10:07.340 --> 00:10:09.370
<i>You have to be a lone wolf!</i>

00:10:10.270 --> 00:10:11.410
<i>Like Ono is!</i>

00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:17.110
<i>It's a lonely place.</i>

00:10:18.280 --> 00:10:21.950
SHIBUYA

00:10:26.090 --> 00:10:27.990
<i>This is one brutal town.</i>

00:10:30.460 --> 00:10:33.290
<i>I came to Shibuya looking for my own turf.</i>

00:10:33.930 --> 00:10:37.630
<i>As usual, the smell of danger here
reminds me of Metro City.</i>

00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:42.500
-The fuck are you doing?
-Fuck off, prick!

00:10:42.570 --> 00:10:45.470
<i>But for me in my sullen mood,
it feels just right.</i>

00:10:49.610 --> 00:10:53.280
<i>It's been a while since I left
my home turf in Mizonokuchi.</i>

00:10:53.350 --> 00:10:56.180
<i>Anyway, when it comes to arcades
in Shibuya, this is the place.</i>

00:10:56.250 --> 00:10:58.120
<i>Shibuya Kaikan Monaco.</i>

00:10:59.920 --> 00:11:03.090
<i>From the basement to the fifth floor,
it's packed with games.</i>

00:11:03.560 --> 00:11:05.660
<i>I could stay here all day
without getting sick of it.</i>

00:11:07.130 --> 00:11:09.660
<i>This place is a battlefield
for formidable gamers.</i>

00:11:09.730 --> 00:11:13.570
<i>I'll spend all my time at fighting games
to motivate me to defeat Team Mizonokuchi.</i>

00:11:14.070 --> 00:11:17.410
Go! Kill him! Kick the General's ass!

00:11:18.840 --> 00:11:21.040
<i>Taito's </i>Global Champion<i>, is it?</i>

00:11:21.610 --> 00:11:25.680
Goddamn, he's tough!
This boss is freaking indestructible!

00:11:25.750 --> 00:11:28.020
He's the most brutal of the brutal!

00:11:28.650 --> 00:11:32.390
<i>If you've met certain conditions,
the final boss is the General.</i>

00:11:33.290 --> 00:11:38.290
<i>His invulnerable fighting style has broken
the spirit of numerous gamers.</i>

00:11:38.730 --> 00:11:39.560
MOST WICKED

00:11:39.630 --> 00:11:43.900
<i>He's so formidable, </i>Gamest<i> says
"sheer will" is the best way to fight him.</i>

00:11:44.900 --> 00:11:47.230
What the hell is with
this three-way flying attack?

00:11:47.300 --> 00:11:49.040
That's so totally unfair!

00:11:49.100 --> 00:11:51.540
That heinous triple-strike sliding kick!

00:11:51.810 --> 00:11:53.870
That awesome anti-jump kick!

00:11:53.940 --> 00:11:57.680
Even when you're far away,
somehow he can grab and throw you!

00:11:58.510 --> 00:12:00.310
And his invincible warp!

00:12:02.320 --> 00:12:07.120
-This boss is just insane!
-Whoever made him is a total sadist!

00:12:07.990 --> 00:12:10.620
-What are you looking at?
-Nothing.

00:12:10.690 --> 00:12:14.860
You're laughing at us for letting
the General take all our 50-yen coins!

00:12:15.300 --> 00:12:16.330
No, I'm not.

00:12:16.400 --> 00:12:19.630
How dare you mock us!
We're going to topple that General!

00:12:19.700 --> 00:12:21.570
I'll tickle the shit out of you, pal!

00:12:21.640 --> 00:12:24.570
If you think you can do it,
then you try it!

00:12:24.770 --> 00:12:27.480
You know what will happen to you
if you don't beat him, right?

00:12:27.540 --> 00:12:29.080
Actually, no, I don't.

00:12:29.540 --> 00:12:31.350
<i>What the heck is going on today?</i>

00:12:31.410 --> 00:12:33.080
<i>I keep getting in trouble
with arcade teams.</i>

00:12:34.420 --> 00:12:37.050
<i>I never thought I would suddenly
be fighting the General.</i>

00:12:37.380 --> 00:12:40.290
<i>If I lose this,
I could get tickled to death.</i>

00:12:41.460 --> 00:12:43.460
So, you're using Wulong, are you?

00:12:43.520 --> 00:12:46.130
Okay, let's see just how far you'll get.

00:12:46.190 --> 00:12:47.430
<i>I'll take down the General.</i>

00:12:48.160 --> 00:12:49.630
<i>Actually, in middle school,</i>

00:12:49.700 --> 00:12:52.070
<i>Ono and I took him on.</i>

00:12:52.630 --> 00:12:55.540
<i>Ono figured out a strategy
for defeating him.</i>

00:12:57.640 --> 00:13:01.410
Ono! If you take down the General,
you'll become a Mizonokuchi legend!

00:13:02.410 --> 00:13:05.080
<i>Unfortunately, she just barely lost.</i>

00:13:05.480 --> 00:13:08.820
<i>Ono, I'm going to take advantage of
that strategy you figured out</i>

00:13:08.880 --> 00:13:11.120
<i>right here and now!</i>

00:13:12.220 --> 00:13:15.360
<i>Do a Ryukizan, then a low kick!
Ryukizan, low kick!</i>

00:13:15.420 --> 00:13:16.920
<i>Ryukizan, low kick!</i>

00:13:18.330 --> 00:13:20.260
<i>-This is unbelievable!
-This is unbelievable!</i>

00:13:20.330 --> 00:13:24.770
<i>That's all! This cunning strategy confuses
the General when he comes in to attack!</i>

00:13:24.830 --> 00:13:28.640
<i>Even Ono could only pummel him
to death with this pattern attack!</i>

00:13:28.700 --> 00:13:30.770
He's got the General on the ropes!

00:13:30.840 --> 00:13:33.410
If you're going to pummel him,
then just keep pummeling!

00:13:33.810 --> 00:13:37.650
I knew this guy couldn't be beaten
with normal attacks.

00:13:38.510 --> 00:13:40.010
Who cares how he does it?

00:13:40.080 --> 00:13:43.080
We just want to see the General go down!

00:13:43.180 --> 00:13:44.520
<i>Ryukizan, low kick!</i>

00:13:45.120 --> 00:13:47.090
<i>Ryukizan, low kick!</i>

00:13:47.150 --> 00:13:49.960
<i>Focus! Stay detached like a robot
when you do your moves!</i>

00:13:50.660 --> 00:13:52.990
<i>I'll overcome the barrier
that Ono could not...</i>

00:13:53.060 --> 00:13:57.530
<i>No! I'll carry out Ono's will
right here and now!</i>

00:13:57.600 --> 00:13:59.300
-Pummel him!
-Pummel him!

00:14:05.610 --> 00:14:07.170
-Awesome!
-Awesome!

00:14:07.240 --> 00:14:11.280
Tell me this isn't a dream!
We'll actually see the General fall!

00:14:11.750 --> 00:14:15.280
When the General falls,
the General's base collapses?

00:14:15.350 --> 00:14:18.620
The General and the General's base
must have been one and the same.

00:14:18.690 --> 00:14:20.820
SURPRISING THAT THE GENERAL FELL.
WE'LL RETREAT FOR NOW,

00:14:20.890 --> 00:14:23.190
BUT HE'S MERELY A VANGUARD.
YOU HAVEN'T SEEN OUR REAL POWER.

00:14:23.260 --> 00:14:26.330
<i>I did it, Ono. Thanks to you,
I made it through...</i>

00:14:26.390 --> 00:14:27.630
That was awesome, man!

00:14:27.700 --> 00:14:29.500
You're no pushover, dude!

00:14:29.560 --> 00:14:32.070
Looks like you've got potential.

00:14:32.130 --> 00:14:34.570
<i>I wish I could have shared this with Ono.</i>

00:14:35.940 --> 00:14:37.400
Okay, newbie!

00:14:38.310 --> 00:14:41.240
Why don't you join us
as part of Team Shibuya?

00:14:41.680 --> 00:14:42.540
Team Shibuya?

00:14:43.010 --> 00:14:47.150
Actually, we heard that some outsiders are
coming in to take over this place.

00:14:47.580 --> 00:14:51.650
We won't stand for it,
so we're looking to gather some allies.

00:14:52.390 --> 00:14:53.520
Outsiders?

00:14:54.120 --> 00:14:56.460
-Team Mizonokuchi!
-Team Mizonokuchi?

00:14:57.190 --> 00:15:01.830
<i>Those jerks! It was stupid of them
to push out the great Yaguchi!</i>

00:15:02.530 --> 00:15:05.600
<i>And I can't stand the fact that
Hidaka is one of them!</i>

00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:09.500
How about it? Want to help us
kick Team Mizonokuchi's ass?

00:15:11.370 --> 00:15:13.670
<i>What? A competition with Team Shibuya?</i>

00:15:14.140 --> 00:15:15.880
I didn't know about this.

00:15:16.340 --> 00:15:18.710
They may not look it,
but they get temperamental.

00:15:18.780 --> 00:15:21.980
It seems they were upset over
being treated like outsiders in Shibuya.

00:15:22.050 --> 00:15:23.580
Why cause trouble like that?

00:15:24.080 --> 00:15:26.020
I don't want to be
in a competition like that.

00:15:26.490 --> 00:15:30.890
Lately, it's popular for teams
from different areas to compete.

00:15:30.960 --> 00:15:35.230
It's also a great way to meet
more people from different places.

00:15:35.300 --> 00:15:37.230
It seems more like just a fight to me.

00:15:37.830 --> 00:15:39.130
<i>What is with this?</i>

00:15:39.200 --> 00:15:43.040
<i>I don't want to get into turf wars
with other gamers.</i>

00:15:43.240 --> 00:15:45.310
<i>I'm totally not into this.</i>

00:15:46.140 --> 00:15:47.940
<i>Street Fighter Alpha 2</i>! This is different!

00:15:48.410 --> 00:15:50.910
-I'm using Rolento, man!
-I'll use Gen!

00:15:50.980 --> 00:15:52.180
I'll be using Rose.

00:15:52.710 --> 00:15:55.880
-But we really want to use Sakura, right?
-But we really want to use Sakura, right?

00:15:57.220 --> 00:16:00.020
<i>Lately, Yaguchi doesn't
come around here anymore...</i>

00:16:00.550 --> 00:16:02.220
<i>even though </i>Street Fighter Alpha 2<i> is out.</i>

00:16:05.260 --> 00:16:07.190
<i>I want to apologize for the other day,</i>

00:16:07.700 --> 00:16:09.330
<i>but I can't really go to his house.</i>

00:16:10.100 --> 00:16:12.430
<i>I just can't bring myself to do it.</i>

00:16:16.770 --> 00:16:19.970
Haruo, you sure have let Shibuya
rub off on you.

00:16:20.440 --> 00:16:22.180
Look at you sitting on the ground.

00:16:22.380 --> 00:16:24.280
It hasn't rubbed off on me!

00:16:24.650 --> 00:16:27.110
I just heard it was okay
to sit on the ground in Shibuya.

00:16:27.180 --> 00:16:30.680
What's with that outfit of yours?
That's so unlike you.

00:16:30.750 --> 00:16:32.890
The Team Shibuya guys gave it to me.

00:16:33.420 --> 00:16:36.320
Those lame clothes you always wear
suit you so much better.

00:16:36.520 --> 00:16:38.890
-The hell?
-Did you hear that?

00:16:38.960 --> 00:16:42.430
-I knew it! You're a Shibuya denizen!
-I'm not!

00:16:45.500 --> 00:16:49.440
<i>Dang! The music in </i>Darius Gaiden<i>
is the bomb!</i>

00:16:49.900 --> 00:16:52.640
I'm no good at shooting games,
but even I'm hooked.

00:16:53.070 --> 00:16:59.210
I can't finish it in one coin yet,
but my route is A, C, F, I, N, S, X!

00:16:59.280 --> 00:17:02.950
<i>Thank goodness. At least
you're still the same in this way, Haruo.</i>

00:17:04.590 --> 00:17:07.620
I got dragged to another one of
these amusement joints!

00:17:07.690 --> 00:17:10.360
Me, an honor student!

00:17:10.420 --> 00:17:11.630
What bullshit!

00:17:12.190 --> 00:17:15.000
I bet this thing never lets you win!

00:17:15.060 --> 00:17:16.000
Total nonsense!

00:17:16.700 --> 00:17:18.470
<i>Girls lately are pretty crazy.</i>

00:17:18.930 --> 00:17:22.340
<i>What the heck is with those socks?
They look like living creatures.</i>

00:17:22.400 --> 00:17:23.940
This totally pisses me off!

00:17:26.070 --> 00:17:30.210
Well, Haruo, I understand why you're upset
over getting bullied by Team Mizonokuchi.

00:17:30.680 --> 00:17:33.810
But that's no reason
to hang out in Shibuya.

00:17:33.880 --> 00:17:36.980
I mean, we came here today
because we're worried about you, man.

00:17:37.420 --> 00:17:41.090
It's okay. There's no reason to be
so afraid of Shibuya.

00:17:41.160 --> 00:17:42.690
There are lots of nice people here.

00:17:43.160 --> 00:17:45.760
That guy playing <i>Treasure Hunt</i>
over there is Shibuya Drill.

00:17:46.530 --> 00:17:49.230
That's Taro. He loves <i>Puzzle Bobble 2</i>.

00:17:50.400 --> 00:17:53.470
Then there's Jason from abroad.
They're all nice guys.

00:17:53.970 --> 00:17:55.600
Are they actually nice people?

00:17:56.540 --> 00:18:00.870
Anyone who loves <i>Treasure Hunt</i>
or <i>Puzzle Bobble 2</i> isn't bad!

00:18:00.940 --> 00:18:05.710
Haruo! As long as you're here,
you'll never see Ono in Mizonokuchi!

00:18:06.310 --> 00:18:09.720
So? It's not like I go to arcades
to run into her.

00:18:10.050 --> 00:18:13.720
Besides, she hasn't come to
the arcades lately.

00:18:15.290 --> 00:18:17.060
Help... Help me!

00:18:18.130 --> 00:18:20.160
What happened to you, Doi?

00:18:20.230 --> 00:18:23.260
Outside, I was a victim of
Air Max snatching.

00:18:23.730 --> 00:18:25.170
Air Max snatching?

00:18:25.230 --> 00:18:28.200
-And jeans snatching too.
-Jeans snatching?

00:18:28.270 --> 00:18:32.610
And the ice cream bar I was eating
was a victim of ice cream bar snatching.

00:18:32.670 --> 00:18:34.880
What? Who the heck did that?

00:18:34.940 --> 00:18:38.450
Come to think of it, the jeans
that guy was wearing are so lame.

00:18:39.610 --> 00:18:43.120
Hey, you! Quit committing
these diabolical deeds!

00:18:43.180 --> 00:18:46.620
You guys are ruining the image of arcades!

00:18:46.690 --> 00:18:49.090
That's right! That's so darn right!

00:18:49.160 --> 00:18:51.190
What? That's such total nonsense.

00:18:51.260 --> 00:18:53.330
What the hell are you so ticked off about?

00:18:53.390 --> 00:18:55.060
That's so FL.

00:18:55.860 --> 00:18:58.270
-What's "FL"?
-It means "fucking lame."

00:18:58.330 --> 00:19:00.230
Are you nuts?

00:19:00.300 --> 00:19:05.070
You're the ones who are FL for pulling off
a high-school boy's jeans.

00:19:05.140 --> 00:19:06.240
That skewers my duck!

00:19:06.310 --> 00:19:09.180
-What her duck?
-It means you've really ticked her off.

00:19:09.240 --> 00:19:11.210
What language are they speaking?

00:19:11.280 --> 00:19:13.980
You goddamn Akihabara boys!

00:19:15.380 --> 00:19:18.590
Any more bullshit lip from you
and I'll blow my top!

00:19:18.650 --> 00:19:20.390
-It's already blown!
-You there.

00:19:20.450 --> 00:19:23.390
-Stop your fighting.
-Who's this?

00:19:23.460 --> 00:19:24.490
Lau?

00:19:25.430 --> 00:19:26.890
Mr. Numata!

00:19:26.960 --> 00:19:31.530
These boys are my former students.
Let them go.

00:19:31.600 --> 00:19:34.070
You're a teacher?
Now, this is a total joke!

00:19:34.130 --> 00:19:39.510
I'll kick your asses, take your money,
and go to a karaoke bar in Shibuya!

00:19:42.210 --> 00:19:43.140
<i>Senpuuga!</i>

00:19:44.410 --> 00:19:45.480
She launched him!

00:19:46.250 --> 00:19:49.350
She's pummeling him with a combo
while he's in mid-air!

00:19:49.920 --> 00:19:54.220
KO! He's done for!
He slid out of the ring!

00:19:54.690 --> 00:19:56.790
What's with the commentary?

00:19:57.220 --> 00:20:00.530
As usual, you're playing around
at an amusement center again.

00:20:00.590 --> 00:20:01.730
Ms. Tono!

00:20:01.800 --> 00:20:04.500
And what the heck is with that outfit?

00:20:04.570 --> 00:20:07.100
You impressed me
during high school entrance exams,

00:20:07.170 --> 00:20:09.900
but you're still the same you, Yaguchi.

00:20:09.970 --> 00:20:10.940
Oh, yes.

00:20:11.000 --> 00:20:14.980
Who cares if you're some schoolteacher?
That won't keep us from brutalizing you.

00:20:15.040 --> 00:20:16.240
They're bad news, Ms. Tono!

00:20:27.720 --> 00:20:31.690
-Awesome!
-I couldn't see what happened at all!

00:20:31.760 --> 00:20:33.690
Goddamn it! We'll get you for that!

00:20:33.760 --> 00:20:35.460
Why you little punks!

00:20:35.530 --> 00:20:38.400
-Round two will be--
-Shut your mouth!

00:20:38.470 --> 00:20:41.170
-All right.
-What is a student's duty?

00:20:41.940 --> 00:20:43.700
-Studying.
-Yes.

00:20:43.770 --> 00:20:46.370
That's 80 percent studying,
20 percent playing!

00:20:46.440 --> 00:20:50.680
It's more like 100 percent playing
in your case, Yaguchi.

00:20:50.740 --> 00:20:53.580
You've got it all wrong!
They tried to help me!

00:20:54.050 --> 00:20:57.580
In fact, instead of abandoning me,
they fought for me! Give them praise!

00:20:58.250 --> 00:21:01.320
My, you two sure care a lot
about your friend.

00:21:01.790 --> 00:21:03.960
-Friend?
-Friend?

00:21:04.790 --> 00:21:06.030
Why you...

00:21:07.530 --> 00:21:09.500
-Farewell.
-Goodbye.

00:21:11.060 --> 00:21:14.270
Haruo, Shibuya really is
a frightening place.

00:21:14.330 --> 00:21:16.970
We're heading on back to Mizonokuchi.

00:21:27.710 --> 00:21:28.880
Hey, Haruo!

00:21:29.380 --> 00:21:31.850
We just met with the guys
from Mizonokuchi.

00:21:31.920 --> 00:21:33.090
Okay...

00:21:33.150 --> 00:21:37.320
We told them who our members are
and discussed what games we'll be playing.

00:21:37.390 --> 00:21:39.930
It's going to be <i>Street Fighter Alpha 2</i>,

00:21:39.990 --> 00:21:42.360
<i>Samurai Shodown III</i>, and <i>Fighting Vipers</i>.

00:21:42.430 --> 00:21:45.330
Someone also suggested
a cotton-candy-making competition.

00:21:45.400 --> 00:21:46.800
What the heck is that?

00:21:46.870 --> 00:21:49.600
What's this game? Are you fighting fish?

00:21:50.000 --> 00:21:51.570
Are there sunfish in it?

00:21:51.770 --> 00:21:54.010
-It's...
-I want to watch!

00:21:59.180 --> 00:22:01.680
Yaguchi is a member of Team Shibuya?

00:23:37.880 --> 00:23:40.950
<i>The two teams battle it out
in Shibuya Center-Gai!</i>

00:23:41.010 --> 00:23:44.650
<i>But it's not just kicks and punches.
They even break out weapons!</i>

00:23:44.720 --> 00:23:47.520
<i>What? A skateboard and an electric guitar?</i>
